Error [jet.InvalidScreen]: `.screen("/tasks/:id", …)` registers no screen: the field `tab` of `TaskView` is neither a `:tab` segment of the path nor marked `#App.Query`.
  --> Tests/UI/app_screen_field_not_in_address.jet:10:56
    |
 10 | graph: fn() -> app.App Never! { app.new("Crew").screen("/tasks/:id", task_screen) }
    |                                                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A screen's state is its address: each of its fields is a `:field` segment of the path or, marked `#App.Query`, goes after `?`, and every target opens the screen from that address, so the state has one screen and each field a place in the address.
 Fix: Write the path as a string literal starting with `/`, give the view one parameter besides its `app.Remote<S>` ones, a struct whose fields each derive `Encode`, name each field that isn't `#App.Query` once as a `:field` segment, and register each state at one screen.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2820
